{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/315852-thrysus-mage-joining-a-pack-lodge-possible","id":315852,"title":"Thrysus Mage Joining a pack / lodge possible?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Werewolf: The Forsaken"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-11-18T20:26:05-08:00","id":315852,"title":"Thrysus Mage Joining a pack / lodge possible?","content":"So its come up that our crossover game has a budding werewolf and a newly awakened thrysus mage. In the absence of any mages, this mage player is considering asking to join his companion's tribe, the pair being introduced to the Storm Lords and the Lodge of the Maelstrom. While he is not part spirit, could the mage join anyway? Through his Spirit magic, he can interact and deal with the Shadow, there is talk of finding a Totem for them as well.<br /> <br /> Is there a mechanical way he can join? If not, can he be an honorary member depending on the situation? Would be interested in hearing your thoughts! Thanks in advance!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1614-berdryn","name":"Berdryn","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"63"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-18T21:35:05-08:00","id":315906,"title":"","content":"At the moment there are no rules for anyone joining a pack (that I know of). 2nd edition is going to have some rules about adding non-uratha to packs, but no non-uratha could ever join a tribe or lodge.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2861-nyx","name":"Nyx","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2861_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"261"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-18T22:07:03-08:00","id":315918,"title":"","content":"You could make a case for it if you had a fairly lenient storyteller.<br /> <br /> The Totem merit is what you need to mechanically join a pack. It has no official prerequisites, but all the merits in that section are listed as &quot;designed for werewolves in particular, and represent edges unavailable to ordinary humans.&quot; Some Changing Breeds explicitly get access to it through Aspects and a bloodline of vampires called the Dead Wolves can take it if they have points in their special discipline Sublunario, so there is a precedent.<br /> <br /> If I was running it and the player was hellbent on the concept I'd tie it to an attainment of a Legacy.<br /> <br /> As for the Tribes...No. Well more specifically you wouldn't get any mechanical benefit from it (since you can't gain Gifts or Renown) and I doubt the 'community' of werewolves would accept you to any degree. You can expect most werewolves to be hostile to the idea for the same reason mages would freak out if a werewolf claimed membership in one of the Orders.<br /> <br /> The best you could hope for is an endorsement from one of the Firstborn if you're super awesome enough to warrant their interest. Spirits sometimes do that just kind of in general, but they're all...what, rank 7 I think? Good luck with that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2079,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2079-red-9","user":"Red 9","date":". 11-19-2014, 01:10 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2079-red-9","name":"Red 9","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2079_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"89"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-18T23:02:22-08:00","id":315960,"title":"","content":"IMO:<br /> <br /> Pack - yes, as part of the extended pack structures of 2nd ed. Socially, he'd probably be held equal (but more powerful) to the wolf blooded. <br /> <br /> He couldn't join a tribe or a lodge. No First Born or lodge totem would sanction that.<br /> <br /> But, in your own game, if the Storyteller likes the idea and allows it, do it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-19T00:11:41-08:00","id":315979,"title":"","content":"It would be roughly akin to asking if a werewolf could join a Legacy... just not going to happen, because the supernatural natures involved aren't really compatible in that sense. In a social sense, I could see the outside supernatural character being considered an associate/fringe member or something of the group in question, but mechanically? It just doesn't mesh.<br /> <br /> Now joining a pack or cabal, I agree works better. Or at least more simply.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/747-knowbody","name":"Knowbody","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"391"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-19T02:53:47-08:00","id":316100,"title":"","content":"I'll say the mage could be part of a pack,<i> with the 2nd edition rules.</i><br /> The new rules about packs seems to be one of the best news about the game.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#800000\">-'' </span>We are the unsullied.<br /> We are the inheritors.<br /> We are the Pure <span style=\"color:#800000\">''-</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3773-helur","name":"Helur","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3773_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"352"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-19T05:11:15-08:00","id":316171,"title":"","content":"As said above 2nd edition will allow non Uratha join packs so joining a pack shouldn't be a problem. Canonically speaking Tribe and Lodge are right out (but it is your game so if it fits better you can always decide differently), but for lodges I was thinking shouldn't it be possible to have an organisation that from the Uratha perspective is a Lodge but from the mages perspective is a Legacy I am not sure how it would work exactly (not to familiar with Legacies and a long time ago since I cracked open my Werewolf books) but I think it would be a nice idea for a cross over game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2735-dutch_wolf","name":"Dutch_Wolf","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-19T16:10:19-08:00","id":316604,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bunyip</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/315852-thrysus-mage-joining-a-pack-lodge-possible?p=315960#post315960\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">He couldn't join a tribe or a lodge. No First Born or lodge totem would sanction that.</div> </div> </div> </div>Are you so sure Bunyip? After all, there are plenty of examples in established lodges of the patrons being whimsical, or changing their mind after a brutal demonstration of faith. Now, I doubt they could ever join a tribe, but I still think a case could be made for a lodge, particularly one such as Lodge of the Union or Lodge of the Savior","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/444-dessembrae","name":"Dessembrae","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar444_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"362"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-19T19:39:08-08:00","id":316877,"title":"","content":"If you want to modify, alter or go around the rules of the game, then anything is possible. As written you have to be Uratha or equivalent to join a lodge or a tribe. Thems the brakes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2861-nyx","name":"Nyx","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2861_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"261"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-19T21:12:46-08:00","id":316913,"title":"","content":"As Bunyip is a writer.... &gt;.&gt; I'm inclined to fall to their official notions on how its to be interpreted. But they also said that you can house rule it however so there's that too.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> WoD-Dark Eras!! (Backed for Viking Age Werewolf)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1939-lyrics-of-war","name":"Lyrics Of War","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1939_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1769"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-19T23:13:48-08:00","id":316991,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dessembrae</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/315852-thrysus-mage-joining-a-pack-lodge-possible?p=316604#post316604\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Are you so sure Bunyip? After all, there are plenty of examples in established lodges of the patrons being whimsical, or changing their mind after a brutal demonstration of faith. Now, I doubt they could ever join a tribe, but I still think a case could be made for a lodge, particularly one such as Lodge of the Union or Lodge of the Savior</div> </div> </div> </div>Two caveats - 1) Do whatever you want in your games, I know I do. 2) Lodge structures haven't been set in stone yet, so what I write here may be completely incompatible with what eventuates. (although I appreciate Lyrics' vote of support).<br /> <br /> Now, in second edition the pack is opened up to allow outsiders to be part of werewolf social structures. This makes sense because Uratha see the world in terms of pack and not-pack. They don't have allies, they have pack. They don't have contacts, they have not-pack who sometimes help them. (This isn't the same as predator and prey - Uratha can have not-pack that they don't regard as prey... yet.)<br /> <br /> So, the pack has a core of werewolves, a grey-area middle ring of wolf-blooded, other supernaturals, and particularly trusted humans, and an outer ring of everything else. (Everything else includes humans, other supernaturals as well, and wolf-blooded who aren't trusted enough to be in the middle. People in the outer ring may not even know they're part of the pack, but the werewolves view them that way, and they're under that pack's protection/authority.)<br /> <br /> So, to my thinking, with the pack now extended to more than just werewolves, lodges are the structures just for werewolves. The pack knows the score, protects the territory, and support the Uratha.They know, but most of them don't <i>really know</i>.<br /> <br /> The lodges <i>really know</i>. This is where werewolves gather with other werewolves who get them. They share similar ideals, burdens, goals, paths, whatever. If I may use a slightly tortured light analogy: Auspice provides the quality of moonlight that illuminates the Uratha's view of the world, tribes are the filters that allow through the particular colours through which the Uratha broadly interprets her purpose, but lodges are lenses that really focus and define that purpose and bring the specific meaning to life that the Uratha is searching for.<br /> <br /> Lodges are the domains of the half-spirits. They're where everyone hunts the same. The lodge founders defined what they believed and they found a patron spirit who embodied that, and now that spirit defines what the Uratha believed and brings others who believe the same under its influence.<br /> <br /> Lodges can bring together different origins (combinations of auspice and tribe) to the same purpose, or even more rarely, bridge the immense gap between Uratha and Anshega and bring them together in one specific purpose and viewpoint.<br /> <br /> For a spirit to allow non-werewolves would be a pollution of the reason for lodge existence. Non-werewolves <i>don't really know</i>. They may have power, they may control spirits through a higher understanding of the supernal, but werewolves are creatures of the fallen world. No-one else fully knows what it is to be werewolf. Most lodges would quickly fall apart with the loss of focus if it brought in outsiders.<br /> <br /> That said, there probably are some very rare lodges that came about to be inclusive and allow outsiders entry. These lodges are probably viewed with some suspicion by most werewolves as being, well, non-werewolfy. Although they were never really human, werewolves are products of their human upbringings and all the prejudices and suspicions that brings.<br /> <br /> Back to the original point, the Thyrsus mage doesn't really know. He can never really know. No magic ability will ever let him truly know what it means to be Uratha. No matter how well he understands the shadow and spirits and shapeshifting and power, <i>his understanding will never be that of the werewolf</i>. And therefore he will never belong in a lodge.<br /> <br /> I'll finish by repeating the caveats once again. Do whatever you want in your games, and take all of this unofficially as lodges haven't been set in stone yet, and until they do everything is speculative.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":9}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-20T08:53:17-08:00","id":317419,"title":"","content":"See the Awakening Blog about Thyrsus (&quot;Invisible Pulse&quot;) for second edition Awakening and how a Spirit mage reacts differently to the <i>hisil</i> than an Uratha.<br /> <br /> There's nothing stopping a mage from being a packmember. They can't join tribes or lodges, though.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Dave Brookshaw</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14-dave-brookshaw","name":"Dave Brookshaw","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar14_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2081"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-20T09:42:42-08:00","id":317470,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bunyip</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/315852-thrysus-mage-joining-a-pack-lodge-possible?p=316991#post316991\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">SNIP! <br /> Back to the original point, the Thyrsus mage doesn't really know. He can never really know. No magic ability will ever let him truly know what it means to be Uratha. No matter how well he understands the shadow and spirits and shapeshifting and power, <i>his understanding will never be that of the werewolf</i>. And therefore he will never belong in a lodge.</div> </div> </div> </div>*slow clap with emphatic head nod*<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/444-dessembrae","name":"Dessembrae","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar444_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"362"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-21T13:18:57-08:00","id":318435,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bunyip</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/315852-thrysus-mage-joining-a-pack-lodge-possible?p=316991#post316991\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Back to the original point, the Thyrsus mage doesn't really know. He can never really know. No magic ability will ever let him truly know what it means to be Uratha. No matter how well he understands the shadow and spirits and shapeshifting and power, <i>his understanding will never be that of the werewolf</i>. And therefore he will never belong in a lodge.</div> </div> </div> </div>I will strongly agree with pack point. With Tribe interpretation, I would probably let a Wolf Blooded Thyrsus to be part of Tribe, if First Born would agree - very big <b>if</b>. ( Other question is still question could Thyrsus to be Wolf Blooded in his character history? ) But as to joining Lodge I have other answer - mage cannot be part of Lodge, it's true. He just don't get it fully. But nothing say's that Lodge's spirit Totem cannot adopt a mage, as his &quot;other child&quot;. In <b>Mage</b> there were Legacies based on idea of spirits or ghosts patrons - why not do something like this?<br /> <br /> Thyrsus PC come to terms with Lodge Totem, taking his patronage as basis of his own Legacies Attainments. He will closely co-work with werewolves on mission of Lodge, because the objects of it are probably very similar to the objects of the Totem spirit. Still, they will be separated, from time to time. Uratha will have their &quot;sacred rites under moonlight&quot;, and Thyrsus will go in seclusion to &quot;meditate with the spirit's patron on secrets of universe&quot;.<br /> <br /> But in the working group it should work rather nice. Only real problem is that in <b>Mage</b> 1ed you can only make your own Legacy at Gnosis 4...<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/confused.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Confused\" smilieid=\"10\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-22T10:06:06-08:00","id":319040,"title":"","content":"With that reasoning, it doesn't seem like being a Mage would be a requirement at all. A wolf-blooded, mortal, vampire, giraffe, anything could become adopted by a totem.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-22T10:17:49-08:00","id":319045,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/315852-thrysus-mage-joining-a-pack-lodge-possible?p=319040#post319040\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">With that reasoning, it doesn't seem like being a Mage would be a requirement at all. A wolf-blooded, mortal, vampire, giraffe, anything could become adopted by a totem.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's true - beside giraffe, that generally isn't enough intelligent to generate Essence by making actions with accordance to Totems nature.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-22T11:34:15-08:00","id":319100,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/315852-thrysus-mage-joining-a-pack-lodge-possible?p=319045#post319045\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It's true - beside giraffe, that generally isn't enough intelligent to generate Essence by making actions with accordance to Totems nature.</div> </div> </div> </div><a href=\"http://vimeo.com/31873464\" target=\"_blank\">Are you sure about that?</a>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I have decided, after some thought, that I don't really feel happy on these forums. I might decide to come back to post. Who knows - but right now, I'm gone.<br /> <br /> So good bye, good luck, and have a nice day.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1170-amechra","name":"amechra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1170_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2316"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-22T13:26:19-08:00","id":319268,"title":"","content":"Lodges don't need to be that complicated. If a lodge is involved with protecting some area of the savanna from poachers, there's one giraffe that managed to barely escape hunters a long time ago. It recognizes the image of men and the sound of jeeps and the moment it hears them it's off in flight. Other animals react similarly, and so this one giraffe acts to protect the savanna from poachers alongside its mage, vampire, wolf-blooded and mortal lodgemates.<br /> <br /> So here's to hoping that new lodges will be more werewolf-oriented, at the risk of forcing the people who want t